@@ -88,7 +90,14 @@
-     * Not preserved from an existing target: Windows attributes, ACLs and
-     * alternate streams, hard-link identity and symlinks (a symlink at `path` is
-     * replaced by a regular file). POSIX permission bits are kept. Read-only
-     * targets fail with PermissionDenied. On POSIX the temporary file is created
-     * with mode 0600 and receives the final mode (the target's, or 0666 minus the
-     * umask) only once its content is complete. SaveManager (M1) adds metadata
-     * and symlink preservation on top of this primitive.
+     * POSIX metadata. A new file is created like any open(O_CREAT, 0666), so the
+     * umask or the directory's default ACL decides its mode. When a file is
+     * replaced, the temporary file is created 0600 and receives the target's
+     * owner, group and permission bits (set-id bits included) only once its
+     * content is complete, as far as this process may set them: the owner needs
+     * CAP_CHOWN and the group needs membership. Whatever cannot be kept fails safe
+     * rather than widening access: a different group loses the group bits and
+     * S_ISGID, a different owner loses S_ISUID.
+     *
+     * Not preserved from an existing target: POSIX ACLs and extended attributes;
+     * Windows attributes, ACLs and alternate streams; hard-link identity and
+     * symlinks (a symlink at `path` is replaced by a regular file). Read-only
+     * targets fail with PermissionDenied. SaveManager (M1) adds metadata and
+     * symlink preservation on top of this primitive.
